[   16.655] [1;97mWhat went wrong[0m
[   16.655] Immucore checks the OS image against the sha256 recorded for it
[   16.655] before it mounts it, and the check did not pass.
[   16.655] 
[   16.655]   Problem:
[   16.656]     checksum mismatch: the image is not what was written
[   16.656]   Image:
[   16.656]     /sysroot/run/initramfs/cos-state/cOS/active.img
[   16.656]   Expected sha256 (stored in active.img.sha256):
[   16.657]     fb868208d29bbd110048e09557719803b62807d82977543841942d3e3b443b85
[   16.657]   Actual sha256 (computed from the image just now):
[   16.658]     9a2b91dad93472ec4eccf274745df47f157860fd013725b0d65f2e9df7102eec
[   16.658] 
[   16.658]   The image has the size and modification time it was written with but
[   16.658]   different content: the storage corrupted it.
[   16.658] 
[   16.659]   Action: fail (from kernel cmdline)
[   16.659] 
[   16.659] [1;97mHow to fix[0m
[   16.659]   - Reboot and pick the passive or recovery entry in the boot menu.
[   16.660]     Then repair the image with kairos-agent upgrade or reset.
[   16.660]   - To boot this image anyway, edit the boot entry (press e) and add
[   16.660]     image-checksum.verify=warn to the kernel line.
[   16.661]   - A disk that corrupts images can corrupt more: check its health.
[   16.661] 
